{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/pulls/173","id":4811126621,"node_id":"PR_kwDOS_nLtM8AAAABHsP3XQ","html_url":"https://github.com/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/pull/173","diff_url":"https://github.com/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/pull/173.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/pull/173.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/issues/173","number":173,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Round111: qualify audit overhead and confirm the fixed Seed block","user":{"login":"yifanXovo","id":171729629,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjxi3Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171729629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo","html_url":"https://github.com/yifanXovo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yifanXovo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**CONFIRMATION_SUPPORT — `R110_MAIN_36_PLUS_R111_SEED_6`.**\n\nThis freezes a scoped ENS-MB research candidate after all six preregistered Seed1 arms ran once, serially, and passed their original complete-clock caps. Their three M-B/P pairs are **TIE / WIN / WIN** (G20-C2 / G50-R1 / G100-R2), with no severe P regression or Seed0 WIN to current Seed1 LOSS. The immutable R110 main36 supply the twelve main comparisons; these are not forty-two measurements under the new wrapper and add no independent geographic samples. ENS-C remains default and cold P-GRB remains the primary benchmark.\n\nR110 remains **BLOCKED**. Its old arm42 whole time is `3600.7215734999627 > 3600`; native_end is `3571.0120709999464`, audit_end is `3600.707823600038`, and necessary audit alone costs `29.69575260009151`. Its old third Seed pair remains UNEVALUABLE. No tolerance, time truncation, old-result replacement, or cross-wrapper exact speedup is introduced. The full three-pair block was fixed before execution so that all current supplementary comparisons share one admitted wrapper.\n\nThe only measured change is equivalent Python audit work: classify model columns once using the original exact string/suffix rules, and reuse pure parse/duplicate-row Counter data within one arm. Cache keys bind current content SHA and parser/contract source identities; every reuse rehashes bytes. Every call still separately checks actual Seed/nine settings, types, A/B, true-G/cutoff/epoch, returns, cover and provenance. Duplicate A/B rows remain legal under Counter>=1, and `state_01` is never integerized into `state_1`. Finally clears the cache and restores historical functions. R110 PE/DLL, all205 production bindings, twelve original inputs, native argv, models, algorithm, numerical policy and30-second reserve are unchanged; required validation remains inside each whole clock.\n\nThe eight fixed fresh-process Seed replays and two old H100 equivalences pass exact mathematical/unknown-field comparisons. All eight necessary postexit observations meet <=15s; maximum including the measured final metric write is14.5154s. The original instrumented arm42 profile is retained without adding nested phase timers or claiming a precise speed ratio. Counterexamples cover names/suffixes, missing and legal duplicate A/B, types, replaced same-path bytes and valid/invalid current-call scope/settings. Two actual H100 Seed1 CLIs (actual V20/M2, cap120 each) exercise LP/MIP/type/Start/physical/normal-return paths. Their original bytes are retained. The final narrow clock/fee boundary correction has actual retained-raw normal/failure branch receipts and independent admission03; it is explicitly a limited closure, not a second byte-identical native CLI run.\n\n|Current arm|Method|Whole / cap seconds|\n|---|---|---|\n|G20-C2|P-GRB|4.306077581 /900|\n|G20-C2|M-B|4.148141000 /900|\n|G50-R1|M-B|1775.124204139 /1800|\n|G50-R1|P-GRB|1771.318191400 /1800|\n|G100-R2|P-GRB|3575.780920905 /3600|\n|G100-R2|M-B|3584.885090700 /3600|\n\nInherited M-B/P and ENS/P each remain **11WIN/1TIE on the same eleven winning roles**. M-B/ENS remains **5WIN/3TIE/4LOSS**, including severe G50-C1 and G100-R2 costs. R108 C2 is distinct historical evidence of repairing an ENS/P benchmark gap; F5 and all ENS costs stay visible, with no hidden ENS pointwise veto. Main15/17/25/26 import qualification is explicitly derived from original intervals/signed proofs while original blanks, false flags, null clocks and missing returns remain intact. Historical main raw matrices are not re-audited. The contribution map and paper specification preserve implicit integer quantity assumptions, physical objective and cover/termination pseudocode, limited real split exposure, unproved G100-R2 zero optimum, conditional AM interpretation, objective scaling and geographic/synthetic overlap. This is engineering qualification and finite confirmation, not a new solver mechanism or statistical guarantee.\n\nResearch fees are **15/24 conservative starts**, **13 actual processes**, and **11299.309934754972/18000 outer seconds**. Qualification is **6/8 starts**, conservatively **583.7201481292723/600 seconds** including actual exit-observation delay. Failed declared slots are not refunded; native nested seconds are not added again. Zero-Optimize engineering/reviewer times, actual failures and unknown manual time are separately recorded.\n\nIndependent original-root and restored-root reviews both reconstruct the six own physical/model/type/Start/scope/cover/return/clock observations and the layered decision. A new limited carrier was actually exported and restored into an absent destination; primary rebuilding from that restored root exactly matches every current CSV/JSON field. The independent public review also runs from the restored root and imports only the fixed finite main authority. There is no original-root or private-binary fallback, no whole old R110 carrier, and no PE/DLL/license/credential in the package. The actual109336170-byte compressed stream uses two genuine exact-byte parts.\n\nScientific payload is frozen at `b92b27c895043af669e64ae32ef0b232262c3244`; later public/remote observations are separate receipts, not retroactive contents of that carrier. Local final audit SHA is `82d9ec0dfd9612de9064dc1df7b0220a795bc838fe90a1b658c3f1564d810348`; restored-root audit SHA is `d5fc15c34232056633e01fdc686d513b656dd95581a19d502776f28d4a24cc18`. See [final report](results/unified_exact_round111/final_report.md), [evidence map](results/unified_exact_round111/contribution_evidence_map.md), [paper candidate](results/unified_exact_round111/paper_candidate_spec.md), [public recovery](results/unified_exact_round111/public_recovery.md), and [public validation](results/unified_exact_round111/public_validation).\n\nThe two remaining falsifiable questions concern G50-C1 representation versus integer-search trajectory and whether a valid Windows/IO trace can consume the empirical reserve. Missing causal identification and a hard timing bound are explicit. This PR neither starts another solver task nor changes the default, merges the candidate, or declares the full paper benchmark complete.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:17:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T12:24:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e3d73dfe9f1dfe5aa46564ad22b36d0f413c7eb4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yifanXovo/TailoredExac